 "text": "Most freshers apply to 200 jobs and hear nothing back. Here's the difference. 1 rupee of effort on a random portal versus a million on the right one. Number 1. Contrast. Stop spraying. Pick 10 companies that are actually hiring this week. Number 2. Speed. The first 50 applicants get red, everyone else gets archived. And number 3. Proof. One small project beats a long resume. I replaced scrolling with building, and that literally changed my life."
